  "result": "`chunk` is written and passes `npm run fast`, but I haven't committed it. The commit title has to end with a task id in parentheses, and my brief didn't include one. I didn't want to make one up.\n\n- **`src/cli/chunk.ts`:** `chunk<T>(items, size)` returns consecutive groups of `size`, and the last group can be shorter. It throws a `RangeError` if `size` isn't an integer of at least 1, which also covers 0, negative numbers and NaN.\n- **`test/cli/chunk.test.ts`:** four `node:test` cases covering even splits, a short final group, an empty list, and rejection of bad sizes.\n- **`scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`:** I added a weight of 0.1 for the new test file.\n- **Checks:** `npm run fast` passed (biome, boundaries, tsc and the related tests).\n\nWhat is the task id? I'll create a branch off `main` (the changes are on `main`, and the repo's git rules say not to commit there) and commit as `Add a chunk helper for fixed-size groups (<id>)`.",
